# The floor the source already stands on, written down rather than inferred.
#
# The binding constraint is the ES2023 change-by-copy array methods —
# `toSorted`, `toReversed`, `toSpliced`, and `with` — which `packages/ui` uses
# on render paths (the toast viewport, the query tree, the pdf-viewer zoom
# ladder, the map geometry). No build step can lower it: esbuild and SWC
# downlevel syntax, never instance methods, so these ship as written whatever a
# target says. Supporting anything older means a core-js polyfill or giving the
# methods up, not a config change.
#
# `tsconfig.base.json` already compiles to ES2023 and `packages/ui` consumes
# source, so these versions are what the published surface has required since
# the first `.with()` call landed. Raising the floor is free; lowering it is the
# decision this file exists to make visible.
#
# caniuse has no feature id for the change-by-copy methods, so the versions are
# spelled out. Each is the release that shipped them. The mobile ids are listed
# in their own right: caniuse scores them separately, and dropping `and_chr`
# alone takes the query from 91 percent of global usage to 47.

chrome >= 110
edge >= 110
firefox >= 115
safari >= 16.4
ios_saf >= 16.4
opera >= 96
samsung >= 21
and_chr >= 110
and_ff >= 115
android >= 110
